# R.B. Cattell and Behavior Genetics.

**Authors:** Loehlin, John C.

## Abstract
Raymond Cattell's efforts to sort out the relationships of genetic or environmental patterns to personality factors have contributed to behavior genetics. Early writings on the projected decline of intelligence in Britain, studies using Multivariate Abstract Variance Analysis, and other miscellaneous studies on personality factors and mental inheritance are reviewed. (BS)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ306008

